{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact head 0dc8c47a26c364ba27282ab65532962b7c132371 on planner/state-seed-note-20261113, its artifact `notes/2026-11-13-state-seed.md` (fbd02ec3), for request 4893fbfa under promise dfff3158 and review request e04e37ed. The draft answers each of the four required changes of ce85878a and both SS2 notes. Two new statements fail at main 57e893c0. Part 2 of the rule depends on the first, and the start and the restart depend on the second.\n\nRequired change 1: `Unheld` does not reach the client through every reader (section 3, part 2).\n\n- The note says that `Own` throws `Unheld`, that the readers \"cannot take it as absent, refuse on it or skip it\", and that the client catches it. Three catch sites in `packages/derive/src` stop it first:\n  - `run` (`marks.ts:549-555`) wraps whatever a platform rule throws in `RuleFault`. Platform rules receive `Own` (`marks.ts:502`).\n  - `unjudged` (`marks.ts:476-483`) turns each `RuleFault` into `{ result: \"unavailable\" }`. It wraps `judgeAct` (`judge.ts:185`, `191`, `207`), the genesis and delivery judges (`genesis.ts:114`, `120`, `delivery.ts:125`) and four settle paths (`settle.ts:71`, `151`, `166`, `172`). The `RuleFault` of `settle.ts:235-237`, which the table lists under \"It throws\", ends there too.\n  - `readRetainedUses` (`retained-use.ts:131-269`) calls `own(originSeq)`, `own.retainedRow` and `own.retainedBirth` inside `try`, and answers `invalid-use` (`:167`) or `invalid-origin` (`:269`) for any throw.\n- A replica that lacks a held entry therefore reads `unavailable` or `invalid-use` where the scope admits, and the client never sees `Unheld`. That is the silent difference that part 2 exists to prevent.\n- One remedy keeps section 10 and decision 2 as they stand: the replica's `Own` records each `Unheld` it throws, and after each judge or fold call the client reads that record. If the record is not empty, the prediction reads `not-judged` or the fold stops the replica, whatever the call returned. The other remedy, a `derive` that rethrows `Unheld` at each catch site, changes `packages/derive` and needs the kernel review. State the remedy, and add to section 9 item 3: the builder lists each catch site that can wrap a read of `Own`, and the ports of `RetainedOwn` (`retainedRow`, `retainedBirth`), which the `Own` interface of `fields.ts:28-36` does not name.\n\nRequired change 2: the held entries at a start and at a restart (section 7).\n\n- Step 8 gives `loadState` \"the entries from F to T\". `loadState` puts a fixed hash for each held entry, and `MemoryState.putFixedHash` keeps the hash of a kept position below the floor (`state.ts:416-418`). `fixedRowsOf` reads those hashes (`fold.ts:302`, `311-314`). Step 8 must pass every held entry: the genesis entry of step 5, each kept position of step 6 and the entries from F to T. The `Own` of section 9 item 2 needs the same set.\n- The restart keeps \"each entry that it holds at or above the new floor\" and goes to step 7. The new floor keeps up to 4,096 positions below itself (`stateKept`, `floor.ts:86`), and the scope still holds them. A replica that drops them lacks entries that the scope holds. With required change 1 it stops, and without it it can answer differently from the scope. The restart must keep each position that the new seed's floor state lists. The replica held each of them before the floor entry, so the restart needs no extra read. The restart also skips step 4. Name the checks of the new seed that the restart runs.\n\nThe kernel question. I confirm the reading of section 10 for this draft: `loadState` uses `MemoryState`, its `put` methods, `indexItems`, `fixedRowsOf`, `putFixed` and `StateSnapshot`, which `packages/derive` exports today. The seed is runtime storage that replay does not read, and the read sits outside `ScopeApi`. The note names no K item. Required change 1 keeps this reading only with the first remedy.\n\nWhat I read: the whole note at the head, and its diff from b4d060ba. The answers to ce85878a hold at 57e893c0:\n- Change 1: the table is partial, and section 9 item 3 makes the builder's list the authority and adds `context.retained`.\n- Change 2: step 3 of 4.1 gives each `fixedRowsOf` result to `putFixed`, as `sqlite.ts:229` does. 4.1 calls `SqliteStore.all` a precedent for the calls only. Retained copies are read before a fold, or stay unheld.\n- Change 3: `credential` is a member read (`sessions.ts:121`), and `dap clone --archive` fetches the journal refs with the same read token (`docs/operate-a-service.md:357-367`). The seed adds nothing to a member's read, and decision 5 ties the seed to the archive.\n- Change 4: section 7 step 5 reads and checks position 0, and section 8 lists it as checked.\n- SS2 notes: 5.1 makes the seed in the floor entry's turn, and SS2 owns the row of the entry-point inventory.\n\nWhat I checked: main 57e893c0 is an ancestor. Against main, the head changes two paths. `notes/2026-11-13-scope-client.md` equals the approved head c98b9a2c. The artifact covers the state seed note at the head. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, the commit-message check passes (10 checked, 0 flagged), and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests, since the head changes no code.\n\nArchitecture: sound apart from the two required changes. A replica that holds what the scope holds needs no list of safe definitions, and a restart at each floor entry keeps the replica's held set equal to the scope's. Decision 9 defers the fold of a floor entry, which reads every held entry and each retained copy, to O6, and that is the right order.\n\nSecurity: required change 1 is the one finding. A wrong prediction grants nothing, since the scope judges each act again. It still shows a member an answer that the scope does not give.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One note: 5.1 says the seed's head T is the floor entry, but a scope that already has a floor makes its first seed \"before its next turn\", at its head and not at a floor entry. Say that T is the head at which the scope made the seed.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fbd02ec34b0f369807e69b2278e8e8df50c55824","binding":"assigned","head":"0dc8c47a26c364ba27282ab65532962b7c132371","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8cbdd2e7c4e127010d370dd02163e14e2feeb8e5\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dfff31586bb07ff7e0c0be591c9674a11f5af190\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5698b71dfe8e095688b4be6508715f59c7d73180","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}